/* book exam traps: Using the drum diameter as the arm of a rope brake. The arm is the effective radius (D + d)/2, 0.51 m in worked example 2, not 1.0 m. | Forgetting the zero reading of a torque-arm balance, or adding the spring reading in a rope brake. The net force is the reading minus the zero, or W − S. | Dropping the 60. With N in rev/min, BP = 2πNT/60; leaving out the 60 makes the power 60 times too large. With ω in rad/s, use BP = Tω. | Mixing mm and m. A 500 mm arm is 0.5 m, not 500. | Confusing bmep with brake power. bmep is pressure, in bar or Pa; BP is power, in kW. */
